  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find head and tail\n    head_val = None\n    head_pos = None\n    tail_positions = []\n    \n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 5:\n                tail_positions.append((r, c))\n            elif val != 0 and val != 5:\n                # Need to distinguish head from obstacles\n                # Head is the single non-zero, non-5 cell that is adjacent to 5s and there's only one of it?\n                pass\n\n    # Actually, head is the unique element that occurs exactly once and is adjacent to 5s.\n    counts = {}\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                counts[val] = counts.get(val, 0) + 1\n                \n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5 and counts[val] == 1:\n                head_val = val\n                head_pos = (r, c)\n                \n    # Determine direction\n    # The tail 5s form a line. The direction is from head away from tail.\n    # Wait, the tail is BEHIND the head. So direction is head - adjacent_tail.\n    adj_tail = None\n    for tr, tc in tail_positions:\n        if abs(tr - head_pos[0]) <= 1 and abs(tc - head_pos[1]) <= 1:\n            adj_tail = (tr, tc)\n            break\n            \n    dr = head_pos[0] - adj_tail[0]\n    dc = head_pos[1] - adj_tail[1]\n    \n    curr_r, curr_c = head_pos\n    \n    while True:\n        nr, nc = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n        \n        # Check boundary collision\n        bounce = False\n        if nr < 0:\n            dr = -dr\n            nr = curr_r + dr\n            bounce = True\n        elif nr >= R:\n            dr = -dr\n            nr = curr_r + dr\n            bounce = True\n            \n        if nc < 0:\n            dc = -dc\n            nc = curr_c + dc\n            bounce = True\n        elif nc >= C:\n            dc = -dc\n            nc = curr_c + dc\n            bounce = True\n            \n        # Check obstacle collision\n        if grid[nr][nc] != 0 and grid[nr][nc] != 5 and grid[nr][nc] != head_val:\n            break\n            \n        curr_r, curr_c = nr, nc\n\n    # Create output grid\n    out_grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Erase head and 5s\n    out_grid[head_pos[0]][head_pos[1]] = 0\n    for tr, tc in tail_positions:\n        out_grid[tr][tc] = 0\n        \n    # Draw head at final position\n    out_grid[curr_r][curr_c] = head_val\n    \n    return out_grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find head and tail\n    head_val = None\n    head_pos = None\n    tail_positions = []\n    \n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 5:\n                tail_positions.append((r, c))\n            elif val != 0 and val != 5:\n                # Need to distinguish head from obstacles\n                # Head is the single non-zero, non-5 cell that is adjacent to 5s and there's only one of it?\n                pass\n\n    # Actually, head is the unique element that occurs exactly once and is adjacent to 5s.\n    counts = {}\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5:\n                counts[val] = counts.get(val, 0) + 1\n                \n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != 0 and val != 5 and counts[val] == 1:\n                head_val = val\n                head_pos = (r, c)\n                \n    # Determine direction\n    # The tail 5s form a line. The direction is from head away from tail.\n    # Wait, the tail is BEHIND the head. So direction is head - adjacent_tail.\n    adj_tail = None\n    for tr, tc in tail_positions:\n        if abs(tr - head_pos[0]) <= 1 and abs(tc - head_pos[1]) <= 1:\n            adj_tail = (tr, tc)\n            break\n            \n    dr = head_pos[0] - adj_tail[0]\n    dc = head_pos[1] - adj_tail[1]\n    \n    curr_r, curr_c = head_pos\n    \n    while True:\n        nr, nc = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n        \n        # Check boundary collision\n        bounce = False\n        if nr < 0:\n            dr = -dr\n            nr = curr_r + dr\n            bounce = True\n        elif nr >= R:\n            dr = -dr\n            nr = curr_r + dr\n            bounce = True\n            \n        if nc < 0:\n            dc = -dc\n            nc = curr_c + dc\n            bounce = True\n        elif nc >= C:\n            dc = -dc\n            nc = curr_c + dc\n            bounce = True\n            \n        # Check obstacle collision\n        if grid[nr][nc] != 0 and grid[nr][nc] != 5 and grid[nr][nc] != head_val:\n            break\n            \n        curr_r, curr_c = nr, nc\n\n    # Create output grid\n    out_grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Erase head and 5s\n    out_grid[head_pos[0]][head_pos[1]] = 0\n    for tr, tc in tail_positions:\n        out_grid[tr][tc] = 0\n        \n    # Draw head at final position\n    out_grid[curr_r][curr_c] = head_val\n    \n    return out_grid",
